{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843988-homebrew-auspex","id":843988,"title":"Homebrew Auspex","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-08T08:54:24-08:00","id":843988,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Homebrew Auspex","content":"Has anyone written a homebrew auspex that sort of blurs together first edition and second edition?<br /> <br /> I really like the aura reading and telepathy from first edition but the questions and such from second edition. Both have Astral projection of sorts, but could one give more of mind reading ability instead?<br /> <br /> I am looking for something unique for a clairvoyant who was turned and is now focusing on auspex. Just wanted to know if anything had been written yet ( or if anyone wants to take a stab at it. ) Thanks !!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T08:58:52-08:00","id":843989,"title":"","content":"I don't really understand what's the objective of this, and what's wrong with Auspex 2nd edition? <br /> <br /> Auspex 2nd edition, can be interpreted as Aura reading on bojects (and is completely within RAW), and telepathy also does all the same things - get general desires of a character, and allow to dig for thoughts. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T09:23:29-08:00","id":844003,"title":"","content":"Good question... Auspex really isnt my forte. (as you can see ) I havent used it since first edition.<br /> <br /> I suppose Lay the mind is a lot like telepathy. It wouldnt really effect the game at all if Auspex was auras instead of like marionette strings or smells or visions of daggers. In the first edition auspex it allowed you to have better sight/senses as such, that seems to be gone in the 2nd one. <br /> <br /> Instead of astral projecting would there be something more mind orientated?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T09:32:49-08:00","id":844006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843988-homebrew-auspex#post843988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone written a homebrew auspex that sort of blurs together first edition and second edition?<br /> <br /> I really like the aura reading and telepathy from first edition but the questions and such from second edition. Both have Astral projection of sorts, but could one give more of mind reading ability instead?<br /> <br /> I am looking for something unique for a clairvoyant who was turned and is now focusing on auspex. Just wanted to know if anything had been written yet ( or if anyone wants to take a stab at it. ) Thanks !!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see much difference between 1e Auspex and 2e Auspex, to be honest. The biggest difference is the first dot. In 1e it enhancing the vampire's mundane senses. In 2e, every vampire has partially enhanced senses as part of the template, and there's a one dot Merit anyone can take that further enhances them, pretty much replicating 1e Auspex 1. The new Auspex 1 works as a low-level extrasensory impression of the surroundings (&quot;reading the room&quot;, so to speak). Every other level is pretty much the same power, just with cleaner execution.<br /> <br /> Level 2 Auspex, you scrutinize a character with your extrasensory perception and learn things about them like their mood, supernatural template, and if they're a diablerist. In 1e, this was done through a color code that you either had to memorize or keep a chart on hand. In 2e this is done by just directly asking questions out of character and having them answered. My 1e group always used the question and answer method because we didn't like the chart. If you liked the chart, you could just give colors as answers in 2e.<br /> <br /> Level 3 Auspex lets you touch an object and receive extrasensory information about it. In 1e, it was mostly left up to the ST how this actually worked. In 2e, you use questions so you know you're getting the information you're actually looking for. Again, my 1e group had been using the 2e method long before 2e came out. If you liked the ST fiat based visions of 1e, you don't really need any rules to incorporate them into 2e Auspex.<br /> <br /> Auspex 4 lets you communicate telepathically. Frankly, I don't see much difference between the 1e and 2e versions at all.<br /> <br /> Auspex 5 lets you do something like astral projection, but not actually astral, since that word has a different specific meaning within the context of CofD. In 1e it was an invisible projection of your body that went about in Twilight. In 2e, it's your senses that leave your body. There is functionally very little difference here, just a slightly different way of describing the idea of &quot;your consciousness becomes separate from your body and goes around spying on folks on its own.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-08-2016, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T09:43:34-08:00","id":844012,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for this comparison. It helps a lot. I never did like the Projecting. Would you have any tips to making... something more mental in the here and now? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T09:47:30-08:00","id":844016,"title":"","content":"Also Auspex multiplies some Kindred Senses anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V:tR2E pg.91</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Upon<br /> Embrace, a vampire\u2019s sense of smell attunes to the scent of blood.<br /> A vampire can smell the presence of blood from about ten yards<br /> or meters per dot of Blood Potency without rolling. Multiply this<br /> range by her Auspex dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:10:59-08:00","id":844026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843988-homebrew-auspex?p=844012#post844012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you very much for this comparison. It helps a lot. I never did like the Projecting. Would you have any tips to making... something more mental in the here and now? </div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, something like that might be possible. What about something like Beast's Hackles amped up to 11? Like for a scene you're always aware of the general mental state and intentions of everyone around you?<br /> <br /> I think I could throw something together for that, if that sounds appealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:25:15-08:00","id":844037,"title":"","content":"Ohh. I like that! Thank you for the suggestion. would it be like 1 vitae or a willpower to activate instead?<br /> <br /> Also thank you Rani for that. I had forgotten you add auspex to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:38:44-08:00","id":844040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843988-homebrew-auspex?p=844037#post844037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ohh. I like that! Thank you for the suggestion. would it be like 1 vitae or a willpower to activate instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still thinking on the best way to mechanically represent a power like this, but maybe 2 Vitae? I have to go to a rehearsal, but I'll whip something up later tonight and post it here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T11:28:19-08:00","id":844070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843988-homebrew-auspex?p=844026#post844026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, something like that might be possible. What about something like Beast's Hackles amped up to 11? Like for a scene you're always aware of the general mental state and intentions of everyone around you?<br /> <br /> I think I could throw something together for that, if that sounds appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea but I see this kind of powers more appropriate for an elder or ancilla. Why not make a devotion with Beast's Hackles and Blood Potency (maybe at 3-4?) at the cost of 2 vitae per scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T13:00:11-08:00","id":844111,"title":"","content":"The only reserve I have for making it a requirement to have X BP is that none of the other disciplines or devotions require that. (at least, to my knowledge, they dont ) an &quot;Elder&quot; could have a BP 1 if they had been in torpor for a long time.<br /> <br /> It would already be someone with at least 6 exp to have 5 in Auspex. I actually dont see it much different than Awe getting ramped up to Idol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T16:07:16-08:00","id":844190,"title":"","content":"Yes you are right probably. I just tried to enlarge the effect of first power <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-08-2016, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T22:40:53-08:00","id":844356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843988-homebrew-auspex?p=844070#post844070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this idea but I see this kind of powers more appropriate for an elder or ancilla. Why not make a devotion with Beast's Hackles and Blood Potency (maybe at 3-4?) at the cost of 2 vitae per scene?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were going to use this power in my own games, I would probably make it a Devotion. But it sounds like what Vitalis is looking for is a replacement 5 dot power, since they don't care for Twilight Projection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843988-homebrew-auspex?p=844111#post844111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reserve I have for making it a requirement to have X BP is that none of the other disciplines or devotions require that. (at least, to my knowledge, they dont ) an &quot;Elder&quot; could have a BP 1 if they had been in torpor for a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Blood Potency doesn't really work as a requirement for Devotions. Vigor is a good go-to Discipline to require for &quot;this other power, but stronger&quot;. Devotions designed for elders tend to do it with high dot requirements and/or high Vitae costs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/843988-homebrew-auspex?p=844111#post844111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would already be someone with at least 6 exp to have 5 in Auspex. I actually dont see it much different than Awe getting ramped up to Idol.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I conceptualized the power as well. Anyway, here's what I was thinking.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Requirement:</b> The vampire must use Beast\u2019s Hackles.<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> After getting a preliminary sense of her surroundings, the vampire attunes her Beast to detect any deviation from her initial observations. As long as this power is active, the storyteller must tell the player if the answers to any of the questions she has asked using Beast\u2019s Hackles during the scene change. Additionally, she knows if anyone is about to engage in violence before they can act on that intention. She cannot be surprised, and automatically acts at the top of the Initiative order if a fight breaks out unless preempted by a character with supernaturally enhanced speed, such as a vampire using Celerity. The vampire may reflexively activate Uncanny Perception once against anyone who engages her directly (whether in conversation or in violence).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T07:55:27-08:00","id":844506,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:13:10-08:00","id":844581,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would recommend staying away from the Celerity effect. One of the pretty awesome thing about 2e is the complete lack of overlap between different Disciplines. Even the swiss-knife-Protean abilities lack overlap with the abilities of anything else. Either way, with all due respect Charlaquin, I don't really feel that you are adding in anything worthy of a level 5 effect - at best, we're looking at a level 2 effect here at best. <br /> <br /> If we're looking for a replacement for level 5 that's less about projecting your mind outside your body (especially when there are cruac scrying effects that do similar), I would do something that's similar to Lord of the Land and Oubliette, but with all lower level abilities at will across a large area. I would also include a wide scale use of the old devotion Talk of the Town. For those of you unfamiliar with this awesome devotion from Invite Only (awesome yet underused book), it lets you instantly zero in on any conversation OR thoughts that are about you. You can literally hear it anytime someone starts thinking about you. Even the surface thoughts of other vampires, without using a willpower. Ability to stretch your senses anywhere in your territory mixed with the ability to pick up anytime someone is plotting against you? That's sheer gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:48:06-08:00","id":844607,"title":"","content":"I like this too, but I am unfamiliar with anything you just mentioned. I dont think i have even heard of Invite Only. How would you write this up mechanically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}